  "surprise": "P30-family attention sink (a learned, zero-initialised key per head with a zero value, prepended to the keys in all six Peri-LN blocks; 4,801,536 params; cached vs full forward max logit diff 8.3e-7 on CPU) on 115-fable scored 621/635/625 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 115's 639/646/609: exact means 627.00 vs 631.33, -4.33, paired -18/-11/+16, inside the registered -40..+40 range (central +5). Discard. The registered mechanism is NOT supported: the RL start got worse, not better. Round-1 targets solved 644/520/760 (mean 641) vs 718/756/691 (722), round-1 sample acc 0.275/0.166/0.352 vs 0.318/0.301/0.315, round-1 parse failures 13347/21413/7863 of 48,000 (28/45/16%, mean 30%) vs 25/22/18%; seed 1 had a milder form of the round-1 collapses in 104/112/116-fable. RL then caught up: r1->r4 +432/+585/+362 (mean +460 vs 115's +384) to RL-solved 1076/1105/1122 (metric_rl 1101 vs 1106), and the eval frontier did not move (ge10 87/92/98 vs 103/97/89, ge11 16/20/23 vs 25/23/19). Pretraining went as predicted: 4112/4149/4089 steps vs 4204/4218/4263 (-2.6%), final val loss 0.0864/0.0812/0.0820 vs 0.0826/0.0806/0.0792 (minima 0.0757/0.0766/0.0768), held-out greedy 0.984/0.986/0.986. Surprise: the sink was not free at RL time, which the registration did not predict. RL sampling ran 122-200 samples/s across seeds (seed 0: 165-200) vs 115 seed 0's 256-296, and totals were 2114/2226/2239 s vs 1572, so a slow pod could have timed out. Likely cause (not profiled): prepending the sink with torch.cat copies each block's whole KV cache on every decoded token. A copy-free sink (a sink slot preallocated in the cache, or the logit folded into the softmax) would remove that cost, but the worse round-1 start gives no reason to expect it to win.",
